# RULE: UX/UI For Electron React Softphone

This is a mandatory Cursor rule.

UX/UI requirements are defined in:

```txt
docs/softphone/UX-UI-Design-Blueprint.md
docs/softphone/UI-Architecture.md
docs/softphone/UI-Design-System.md
docs/softphone/UI-Component-Catalog.md
```

Read `UI-Architecture.md` before any renderer change (hooks, shells, components, stores).

## UX Before UI

Before implementing a user-visible component define:

- affected `LF-XXX` IDs
- visual states
- loading states
- error states
- disabled states
- recovery states
- accessibility behavior
- test IDs

Do not create React components before state design is clear.

## Component Boundary

React components may:

- render props
- emit callbacks
- compose UI-only hooks
- show projections

React components must not:

- call SIP
- call Electron
- call WebSocket
- call repositories
- own business rules
- parse integration payloads

## Electron UX

Electron shell behavior belongs outside React business logic.

Main process may own:

- tray
- window lifecycle
- native notifications
- app close behavior
- minimize and restore

Renderer may display:

- shell projections
- warnings
- user controls

## Required Global States

The UI must represent:

- booting
- legacy operator authenticating
- legacy operator platform session exists
- legacy operator platform invalid token
- SIP registering
- SIP registered
- SIP registration failed
- DND
- legacy operator platform disconnected
- incoming ringing
- active call
- held call
- transfer mode
- failed operation

## Disabled Controls

Every disabled critical control must have a reason.

Examples:

- not registered
- legacy operator platform reserved
- invalid number
- second session disabled
- DND active
- transfer in progress
- reconnecting

Disabled state must come from projection, not local component guesses.

## Language (Internationalized UI)

All user-visible copy must go through the i18n catalog/runtime (`src/renderer/i18n/*`) for every supported locale (`ru`, `en`):

- labels, buttons, headings, hints, placeholders
- error and policy banners, disabled reasons, tooltips
- `aria-label`, `aria-labelledby`, and live-region messages

Technical identifiers stay English: `data-testid`, projection reason keys, Domain enums.

Do not introduce hardcoded user-visible strings in renderer components, shell hooks, helpers, icon labels, or UI-facing application projections.

New UI work: assert translation keys or localized render output in tests (at least `ru` + `en` for touched surfaces).

## Accessibility

Every interactive control must have:

- keyboard access
- visible focus
- accessible label
- non-color-only state indicator

Critical actions require clear labels:

- answer
- reject
- hang up
- hold
- resume
- mute
- transfer
- retry

## CSS Modules And Tokens (UI-4)

Mandatory for renderer UI work after 2026-06-25 foundation:

- Read `docs/softphone/P11-CSS-Modules-Tokens-Migration.md` before styling changes.
- New or touched `components/**`, `shells/**`, `widgets/**` → co-located `*.module.css` + `var(--*)` from `src/renderer/styles/tokens.css`.
- Do **not** add legacy global component stylesheets; use co-located `*.module.css` + `var(--*)` from `src/renderer/styles/tokens.css`.
- Use `clsx` for conditional/variant classes.

### CSS Modules naming (mandatory)

- **CSS selectors:** kebab-case only — `.row-panel { }`, not `.rowPanel { }`.
- **TypeScript access:** dot notation — `styles.rowPanel`, not `styles["rowPanel"]`.
- Vite `localsConvention: "camelCase"` maps `.row-panel` → `styles.rowPanel`.
- Dynamic variants: `Record<Variant, string>` map (see `RegistrationStatusDot`), not `styles[\`foo_${x}\`]`.
- Enforced by ESLint (`@typescript-eslint/dot-notation`, `no-restricted-syntax`) and Stylelint (`selector-class-pattern`).

## Layout And Scrolling

- Root shell (`App`, `SoftphoneLayout`) must not scroll; use `height: 100vh` and `overflow: hidden`.
- Each layout zone owns its padding (`header`, `context`, `controls`) — no shared outer padding on the root shell.
- Only inner zones may scroll (e.g. `layout-context-zone` for call sessions); controls and header stay fixed-height.

## Color Themes (LF-082)

The app supports **light** (default) and **dark** themes via `data-theme` on `documentElement` and semantic tokens in `tokens.css`.

Mandatory for every `/ui` session that touches visible styles:

- Implement and verify **both** `light` and `dark` — never ship UI styled for a single theme only.
- Use semantic `var(--color-*)` tokens only; no hardcoded hex/rgb in component CSS (shadows: `--shadow-*`).
- Do not branch theme colors in React — switch tokens via `data-theme`, not inline styles.
- Storybook: add or update stories for both themes when changing critical surfaces.
- Settings write path: `theme` in `UserSettings` → `useSettingsActions.onThemeChange` → `applyAppTheme`.

## Icons

- Read `guides/Icon-Agent-Guide.md` and `Icon-Registry.md` before adding icons.
- Use `AppIcon` with semantic id; rule: `.cursor/rules/icons.mdc`, skill: `.cursor/skills/icons/SKILL.md`.
- Icon-only controls: `IconControlButton` + `IconTooltip` (300ms delay); see `handoffs/P11-Icon-Tooltips-Agent-Prompt.md` (done T-001).

## Completion Check

Before finishing UI work verify:

- UX state inventory exists
- component remains presentational
- Use Cases are called outside component internals
- accessibility is covered
- critical call state is visible
- Electron behavior is not mixed with Domain logic
